==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|fersly}}; equivalent to {{suffix|en|fierce|ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/fɪɹsli/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/fɪəsli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-fiercely.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyph|en|fierce|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|er|more}}

# In a [[fierce#Adjective|fierce]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|The wind blew '''fiercely''' and the rain fell heavily.}}
#* {{RQ:Jefferies Amateur Poacher|chapter=1|passage=They burned the old gun that used to stand in the dark corner up in the garret, close to the stuffed fox that always grinned so '''fiercely'''. Perhaps the reason why he seemed in such a ghastly rage was that he did not come by his death fairly. And why else was he put away up there out of sight?—and so magnificent a brush as he had too.}}
#* {{RQ:Doyle Lost World|passage=He helped himself to a cigar and leaned back with a '''fiercely''' critical pair of eyes, taking note of the effect which this document would produce.}}
# [[extremely]]; to a large degree
#: {{coi|en|'''fiercely''' competitive}}
#: {{coi|en|a '''fiercely''' loved woman}}
#: {{coi|en|a '''fiercely''' proud father}}
#: {{coi|en|'''fiercely''' disappointed}}
#: {{coi|en|'''fiercely''' loyal}}
#: {{coi|en|'''fiercely''' independent}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=29 May 2021|author=Phil McNulty|title=Manchester City 0-1 Chelsea
|work=BBC Sport|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/57268064|passage={{w|Thomas Tuchel|Tuchel}} made it three out of three against {{w|Pep Guardiola|Guardiola}} by producing a '''fiercely''' disciplined, positive Chelsea performance that has brought a season that was shrouded in uncertainty to the most glorious conclusion.}}

